      "writtenOn": "2021-06-09T16:51:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This doesn\u0027t seem to quite match the format of https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:packages/modules/Virtualization/microdroid/microdroid_payload.json and parsed by mk_payload.cc. Where is it used, and what\u0027s the difference?",
      "revId": "dab8b438fa55b75d22864b4a9acf4b85351f680e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c11844a9_67a1cbb7",
        "filename": "microdroid/payload/config.proto",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 31,
      "author": {
        "id": 1415877
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-06-09T18:56:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Config for mk_payload is an intermediate format to configure mk_payload while the schema in this change is for the VM payload config, which is what the client would prepare and store within its APK as an asset.\n\nmk_payload\u0027s config might be generated by SDK library or VirtualizationService to invoke mk_payload based on VM payload config. mk_payload\u0027s config doesn\u0027t have to be in JSON. For example, if we merge mk_cdisk and mk_payload into virtualizationservice, then mk_payload\u0027s config would be simply a struct.\n\nYeah, for now, these two share some structural similarity and look a bit confusing. That\u0027s why I uploaded this schema to make them explicit.",
      "parentUuid": "2717502a_23244fd9",
      "revId": "dab8b438fa55b75d22864b4a9acf4b85351f680e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
